OL,3,GNEWSAMore teens with chronic pain think
OL,4,Aof self-harm
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than half of teenagers treated for
OL,7,Fchronic pain have thought about
OL,8,Fself-harm, a study has found.
OL,10,FThe research led by University of
OL,11,FOxford and Oxford University Hospitals
OL,12,FNHS Foundation Trust shows that 58% of
OL,13,Fthe 77 surveyed young people aged 12 to
OL,14,F18 reported lifetime thoughts of
OL,15,Fself-harm, while 47% reported self-harm
OL,16,Fbehaviour.
OL,18,FFindings also show their perceived
OL,19,Fburdensomeness and hopelessness were
OL,20,F"strongly associated" with self-harm
OL,21,Fthoughts and behaviours.
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
